>child process of the parent has no where to respond and
>indicate a termination which results in these ghost
>processes, that you cant kill... I anyone knows how to get
>rid of them, I sure would like some insight.

No, if the parent process properly wait()s the child, this
isn't a problem.  To get rid of zombies (aka "defunct" processes),
kill the parent process.  On Digital UNIX, you can obtain the
parent process ID with "ps O ppid", for example.

